2026-09-28 -- K04b independent completion-event observation.

ublk-trace-order.c retains original fio --name=write_seq --ioengine=libaio
--iodepth=16 --rw=write --size=512M --direct=1 --bs=4k and original seq_io.bt.
It adds an independent tracefs instance of block_rq_issue/block_rq_complete,
filtered to the device, with global clock and bounded per-CPU buffers. It
checks all sectors exactly once, request errors, and overrun/drop counters.
No order condition is imposed on the diagnostic's PASS verdict. Null storage
cannot establish persistence. The upstream test/assertions remain unchanged.

GCC14/Clang19 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror compile PASS, GCC probe executed:
                  original bpf breaks    independent completion breaks
GCC, one queue                 0                         0
EvoCC, one queue               0                         0
GCC, two queues                4                         9
EvoCC, two queues              5                         5
All four cases: 131,072 issued / completed requests; 1,048,576 sectors exactly
once; zero missing/duplicate/error/lost events; fio exits zero; issued requests
are sequential. Both multi-queue traces show sector 128 completing on CPU 0
before sector 64 on CPU 2. The upstream observer reports the same first jump.
The two-queue runs use CPUs 0/2; one-queue controls use CPU 0. The original
observer's global map is not an exact serialized event counter (4 vs 9 on
GCC); nevertheless independent observation proves actual completion reordering,
not merely a bpftrace formatting/mapping artifact. No compiler repair is claimed.

The frozen kublk.c main initializes nr_hw_queues=2. Therefore generic_01's
omitted -q does not mean one queue; generic_02 explicitly requests the same two
queues. Runtime confirmation of that installed binary's default follows in a
separate control. Frozen Documentation/block/blk-mq.rst states no completion
order guarantee; the source-bound diagnosis must include the actual observed
cross-CPU completions, not rely solely on that general documentation.

Both diagnostic TAP populations 2/2 PASS and nonce-bound HVF shutdown PASS.
These are observer/coverage checks, NOT original generic_01/02 PASS. The retained
Images/configuration/QEMU drift are kernel-uniform-selected-runtime.out's
subjects. Runtime hashes remain unchanged; no new full disk or workspace copy.

